AVX-NE-CONVERT: VBCSTNEBF162PS / VBCSTNESH2PS broadcast a word instead of the widened dword, and their opmap prefixes are swapped

Two defects found while diffing an independent model of the AVX-NE-CONVERT
group (the six load-and-widen forms) against the emulator; the SDM (Vol. 2C,
VBCSTNEBF162PS / VBCSTNESH2PS) is the authority for both.

1. VBCSTNEBF162PS_VpsWwM and VBCSTNESH2PS_VpsWshM widen the one 16-bit memory
   element to float32 and then replicate it with xmm_pbroadcastw(), whose
   parameter is a Bit16u: the float32 is truncated to its LOW word and that
   word is broadcast to all eight word lanes. For the bf16 form the low word
   of the shifted value is always zero, so every result was +0.0; for the
   fp16 form it was the low half of the converted mantissa in every word. The
   SDM: "dest.dword[i] = make_fp32(TMP.dword[i].word[0])" /
   "convert_fp16_to_fp32(...)" for i in range(KL) - one f32 per DWORD lane.
   Fixed by broadcasting the dword (xmm_pbroadcastd).

2. The VEX 0F38 B1 opmap group binds prefix 66 to VBCSTNEBF162PS and F3 to
   VBCSTNESH2PS. The SDM encodings are the other way round: VBCSTNEBF162PS is
   VEX.128/256.F3.0F38.W0 B1 and VBCSTNESH2PS is VEX.128/256.66.0F38.W0 B1
   (the B0 group next to it already has F3 = bf16 / 66 = fp16). So a
   vbcstnebf162ps executed the fp16 widen and vice versa. The IA names are
   swapped back; handlers and .def rows were right.

Found 2026-09-14 by the hybrid-x86-oracle differential harness diffing the
zens model of the AVX-NE-CONVERT group. Both are present on upstream master as
of 2026-09-14.

diff --git a/cpu/avx/avx_ne_convert.cc b/cpu/avx/avx_ne_convert.cc
index a3d2a7c..7776649 100644
--- a/cpu/avx/avx_ne_convert.cc
+++ b/cpu/avx/avx_ne_convert.cc
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@ void BX_CPP_AttrRegparmN(1) BX_CPU_C::VBCSTNEBF162PS_VpsWwM(bxInstruction_c *i)
   float32 op = convert_bfloat16_to_fp32(read_virtual_word(i->seg(), eaddr));
 
   for (unsigned n=0; n < len; n++)
-    xmm_pbroadcastw(&dst.vmm128(n), op);
+    xmm_pbroadcastd(&dst.vmm128(n), op); // op is the widened float32, not a word
 
   BX_WRITE_AVX_REG(i->dst(), dst);
   BX_NEXT_INSTR(i);
@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ void BX_CPP_AttrRegparmN(1) BX_CPU_C::VBCSTNESH2PS_VpsWshM(bxInstruction_c *i)
   float32 op = convert_ne_fp16_to_fp32(read_virtual_word(i->seg(), eaddr));
 
   for (unsigned n=0; n < len; n++)
-    xmm_pbroadcastw(&dst.vmm128(n), op);
+    xmm_pbroadcastd(&dst.vmm128(n), op); // op is the widened float32, not a word
 
   BX_WRITE_AVX_REG(i->dst(), dst);
   BX_NEXT_INSTR(i);
diff --git a/cpu/decoder/fetchdecode_opmap_avx.cc b/cpu/decoder/fetchdecode_opmap_avx.cc
index a496458..fbc9862 100644
--- a/cpu/decoder/fetchdecode_opmap_avx.cc
+++ b/cpu/decoder/fetchdecode_opmap_avx.cc
@@ -1180,8 +1180,8 @@ static const Bit64u BxOpcodeGroup_VEX_0F38B0[] = {
 };
 
 static const Bit64u BxOpcodeGroup_VEX_0F38B1[] = {
-  form_opcode(ATTR_SSE_PREFIX_66 | ATTR_VEX_W0 | ATTR_MOD_MEM, BX_IA_VBCSTNEBF162PS_VpsWw),
-  last_opcode(ATTR_SSE_PREFIX_F3 | ATTR_VEX_W0 | ATTR_MOD_MEM, BX_IA_VBCSTNESH2PS_VpsWsh)
+  form_opcode(ATTR_SSE_PREFIX_66 | ATTR_VEX_W0 | ATTR_MOD_MEM, BX_IA_VBCSTNESH2PS_VpsWsh),
+  last_opcode(ATTR_SSE_PREFIX_F3 | ATTR_VEX_W0 | ATTR_MOD_MEM, BX_IA_VBCSTNEBF162PS_VpsWw)
 };
 
 static const Bit64u BxOpcodeGroup_VEX_0F38B4[] = { last_opcode(ATTR_SSE_PREFIX_66 | ATTR_VEX_W1, BX_IA_VPMADD52LUQ_VdqHdqWdq) };
